The environment menu's exit node, server side: keep it with the runner's report.

POST /v1/sessions/{id}/environment/report takes exit_node, the tailnet exit
node the session's repositories name as the runner finds it (runner patch
0012-environment-exit-node.patch): its state (connected, offline, off,
failed, conflict or unknown), its name, the names when the repositories name
different ones, and Tailscale's error when it refused it. GET
/v1/sessions/{id}/environment returns it with the rest of the report, and
leaves it out when there's none, as with a runner from before exit nodes.
Base: omnigent v0.18.0 (a8676d23e88d), after 0020-stop-message-waiting-for-sandbox.patch.
